<div class="faq-section"> <h2>Student Q&A: Medical Pathways After PUC</h2> <details class="faq-item"> <summary>What exams should I write after PUC science in Karnataka for medical?</summary> <p>
To pursue MBBS, BDS, or AYUSH courses in Karnataka, you must write the NEET-UG exam. For Allied Health Sciences, B.Sc Nursing, B.Pharm, and BPT, you should write the KCET exam conducted by KEA.
</p> </details> <details class="faq-item"> <summary>How can I get into a government medical college in Karnataka?</summary> <p>
Admission to government medical colleges in Karnataka is primarily through NEET-UG. You need a high NEET score to secure a seat via the 85% state quota (counseling by KEA) or the 15% All India Quota (counseling by MCC).
</p> </details> <details class="faq-item"> <summary>What are the best alternatives if I don't clear NEET?</summary> <p>
If you don't clear NEET, you have excellent parallel career paths. You can pursue Allied Health Sciences, B.Sc Nursing, Physiotherapy (BPT), or Pharmacy (B.Pharm) through KCET. These paths offer great career growth and stability without the NEET requirement.
</p> </details> </div>

